  "formula": "emissions_kg_CO2e = shipped_units * assumed_gross_mass_kg_per_unit / 1000 * route_distance_km * combined_factor_kg_CO2e_per_tonne_km",
  "notes": [
    "Aviation factors already include 8% distance uplift. Use airport great-circle distance without multiplying by 1.08 again. Source: full-set Freighting goods worksheet, FAQ row 172.",
    "WTT means well-to-tank fuel-supply emissions. Add the matched WTT row once to the operational factor; do not add it again when using the combined factor.",
    "UK reporting averages are scenario proxies for non-UK/Netherlands-Singapore routes, not measured ASML or Marvell emissions.",
    "Without-RF results exclude indirect non-CO2 aviation effects; the official guidance recommends reporting indirect effects as well, noting scientific uncertainty. Include the RF sensitivity.",
    "Physical shipment mass is in tonnes; synthetic SKU masses and warehousing coefficients are separate declared scenario assumptions.",
    "These transport factors do not include semiconductor manufacturing emissions or warehouse electricity."
  ],
